Source: secubox-dns-guard
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Gerald KERMA <devel@cybermind.fr>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2

Package: secubox-dns-guard
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, secubox-core (>= 1.0.0)
Recommends: dnsmasq
Description: SecuBox DNS Guard — anomaly detection + dnsmasq blocking
 Watches recursive DNS resolution for anomalous patterns and pushes
 blocklists to dnsmasq via /etc/dnsmasq.d/secubox-blocklist.conf.
 .
 Distinct from sibling packages in the DNS cluster:
  - secubox-vortex-dns — full recursive DNS firewall with RPZ
    (unbound-backed; inline blocking before resolution).
  - secubox-ad-guard — ad/tracker-specific blocking with per-device
    stats.
  - secubox-dns — authoritative BIND zone manager (publishing).
  - secubox-dns-provider — external registrar API.
